<file path="doc/HARDWARE_DEMO_RUNBOOK.md">
# Aegis-Twin Hardware Demo Runbook

## Topology

Place the attack VM and Raspberry Pi on an isolated host-only/bridged subnet
whose traffic crosses a laptop interface visible to Zeek. Keep the management
API on a separate localhost or management path.

The default identifiers are:

- Device: `PI-001`
- Registered attack job: `pi-syn-demo`
- Example Pi address in the Zeek policy: `192.168.56.20`

Change the `target` constant in `scripts/zeek/aegis-live.zeek` to the real Pi
address before the event.

## Start the telemetry path

1. Start FastAPI on port 8000.
2. Run Zeek on the isolated interface with `scripts/zeek/aegis-live.zeek`.
3. Confirm that Zeek writes JSON records to `aegis_live.log` once per second.
4. Start the forwarder:

   ```bash
   python scripts/zeek_tail.py /path/to/aegis_live.log --job-id pi-syn-demo
   ```

5. Verify `GET /api/v1/devices/PI-001/state` reports `HEALTHY` and trust in
   the 96–99 range.

The packet-level Zeek handler is intentionally limited to the isolated lab
target. It is designed for this low-volume hackathon topology, not a large
production network.

## Attack-controller contract

Set these environment variables on the backend:

```text
AEGIS_ATTACK_CONTROLLER_URL=http://<management-address>:<port>
AEGIS_ATTACK_CONTROLLER_TOKEN=<shared-lab-token>
AEGIS_ALLOWED_ATTACK_JOB_IDS=pi-syn-demo
```

The controller must expose:

```text
POST /jobs/pi-syn-demo/stop
Authorization: Bearer <shared-lab-token>
Content-Type: application/json

{"job_id":"pi-syn-demo"}
```

It must return `{"stopped": true}` only after stopping the process it already
registered under that job ID. The Aegis API never accepts or executes a shell
command from a remediation request.

## Learned artifacts

The repository includes controlled synthetic-demo checkpoints and metrics.
After capturing the real topology, replace them with session-labeled artifacts:

```bash
python scripts/train_hybrid_models.py --input data/pi_sessions.jsonl --epochs 30
python scripts/run_demo_acceptance.py --loops 20
```

Every JSONL row uses the telemetry-window request body and adds `label` and
`session_id`. Keep entire sessions together when recording and validating.

## Backup replay

If hardware capture fails during judging, call:

```text
POST /api/v1/demo/replay/pi_syn?speed=4
```

Replay windows pass through the same engine and SSE path as live Pi telemetry.
